From b10d469f47a3d679aae9a09a657a8c47ca7b1677 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:55:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] diag: add per-evaluation DEBUG log to investigate live
 presence-confirmation gap

Real-world data (son's shower, then a later multi-session day) shows the
Decision Engine reaching delta >= max_humidity_delta (confirmed directly,
since sensor.shower_guard_humidity_delta is published verbatim from
result.humidity_delta -- proving the live evaluate() call entered that
branch) without ever cutting water, even during a window where the
presence sensor's exported history shows it was seemingly on shortly
before/during the crossing. Meanwhile, ADR-0006's presence-corroborated
session-end path (which requires the exact same underlying presence
wiring) has fired correctly and repeatedly the same day.

Existing logging can't distinguish these cases: __init__.py only logs a
decision INFO line when the decision actually CHANGES, so a call that
computes delta >= threshold but doesn't cut (presence unconfirmed)
produces no log output at all -- indistinguishable from a call that
never approached the threshold. There's no visibility into what
`presence` / `last_presence_at` / the computed delta actually were on
the specific call in question.

This is diagnostic-only, no behavior change: _evaluate_and_record() now
logs a DEBUG line on every single evaluation with the exact inputs
(humidity, active_since_humidity, computed delta, presence,
last_presence_at) and the resulting decision/reason. Enable via
`logger: logs: custom_components.shower_guard: debug` in
configuration.yaml. Intended to be removed once the underlying
discrepancy is understood -- flagged as such in the code comment and
README.

- __init__.py: _evaluate_and_record() gains one _LOGGER.debug() call.
  No other behavior changes.
- const.py / manifest.json: version bump only (1.9.1) -- diagnostic
  addition, not an architectural change, so no new ADR.
- Tests: 1 new test in test_init.py using caplog to confirm the DEBUG
  line fires on every evaluation with the expected fields. Full suite:
  120 passed (119 previously passing + 1 new).
- README.md: new "Diagnostic logging (temporary)" subsection under
  Development, documenting how to enable it and that it's safe to
  remove once resolved.
